I participated in the previous round of discussion for this paper (NeurIPS 2025). The main issues were:

1) Poor readability (hard to follow);
2) Over-engineering combined with a lack of motivation for the design choices;
3) Insufficient discussion of other sparse/octree-based autoregressive models;
4) Inappropriate title ("unified").

Unfortunately, these problems persist, although the draft has improved slightly (e.g., Fig 1, Sec 2.2, and Sec 2.3 are much clearer than the last submission).

The comments from the current positive reviewers (scores 8 and 10) are not convincing. All modern 3D generative models focus on sparse modeling and long sequence generation, so this does not make the paper stand out.

Overall, I recommend rejection despite the high scores.
